6PAPRQ1\\nU2 -> imports/ISO7342FCQDWRQ1\\n\\nWhat about Q1? It\'s an NPN.\\nWhat about D1? LED.\\nWhat about RT1-RT8? Thermistors.\\n\\nUsually, for these common components, we might not need specific library imports if they are standard passives, but the instructions say \\"create missing components if necessary\\".\\n\\nLet\'s check if there are any other ICs or specific components.\\nThe SCUD mentions:\\n- U1: TI BQ79616PAPQ1\\n- U2: TI ISO7342CQDWRQ1\\n\\nI\'ll try to find a more exact match for U2 if possible. The SCUD says ISO7342CQDWRQ1. I found ISO7342FCQDWRQ1.\\nLet\'s try searching for ISO7342C."}'}}, {'id': 'call_c286000e010146968fb62dcdc298', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'resolve_component', 'arguments': '{"security_risk": "LOW", "query": "ISO7342C"}'}}]}, {'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'Your thought has been logged.'}], 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_199129b15f5b47abad54dff3aba3', 'name': 'think'}, {'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': "[Tool 'resolve_component' executed.]"}, {'type': 'text', 'text': '{\n  "status": "selection_required",\n  "options": [\n    "ISO7342CDWR (C560965)"\n  ]\n}'}], 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_c286000e010146968fb62dcdc298', 'name': 'resolve_component'}], tools=[{'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'file_editor', 'description': "Custom editing tool for viewing, creating and editing files in plain-text format\n* State is persistent across command calls and discussions with the user\n* If `path` is an image file (.png, .jpg, .jpeg, .gif, .webp, .bmp), `view` displays the image content\n* If `path` is a text file, `view` displays the result of applying `cat -n`. If `path` is a directory, `view` lists non-hidden files and directories up to 2 levels deep\n* The `create` command cannot be used if the specified `path` already exists as a file\n* If a `command` generates a long output, it will be truncated and marked with `<response clipped>`\n* The `undo_edit` command will revert the last edit