PN Transistor (External LDO Pass Element)\\n- Q2: NPN Transistor footprint (DNP)\\n- D1: Green LED\\n- D3: 24V Dual Zener/TVS Diode\\n- RT1-RT8: Thermistors (NTC)\\n\\nIn the VHL Library, I found:\\n- imports/BQ79616PAPRQ1 (Matches U1, though the suffix is slightly different, PAPRQ1 vs PAPQ1, usually R means tape and reel, so it\'s the same part)\\n- imports/ISO7342FCQDWRQ1 (Matches U2, though it\'s the \'F\' version which usually means default output state is different, but it\'s the closest match and likely acceptable for this analysis).\\n\\nI should check if there are other components like the NPN transistor or the TVS diode that need to be created.\\nThe SCUD mentions:\\n- Q1: NPN Transistor.\\n- D3: 24V Dual Zener/TVS Diode.\\n\\nWait, the user asked to \\"Analyze the \'Components Inventory\', check the VHL Library, create missing components if necessary, and update the SCUD file with a \'Library Mapping\' section.\\"\\n\\nI should probably look for a generic NPN transistor and a TVS diode if they are not in the library.\\nActually, for Q1 and D3, the SCUD doesn\'t give specific part numbers, just descriptions.\\nQ1: NPN Transistor (External LDO Pass Element).\\nD3: 24V Dual Zener/TVS Diode.\\n\\nI\'ll check if there are any common NPN transistors or TVS diodes in the library.\\nActually, I should check if I can find more specific part numbers for Q1 and D3 from the SCUD or if I should just use generic ones if available.\\nThe SCUD says:\\n\\"Q1: NPN Transistor (External LDO Pass Element). Active.\\"\\n\\"D3: 24V Dual Zener/TVS Diode\\"\\n\\nLet\'s see if I can find any other components in the library.\\nI\'ll list the local components again to be sure.\\nWait, I only see two components.\\n\\nI\'ll try to resolve a common NPN transistor like MMBT3904 or similar to see if it\'s available.\\nBut the task is to process the SCUD file.\\n\\nLet\'s look at the SCUD file again.\\nU1: TI BQ79616PAPQ1\\nU2: TI ISO7342CQDWRQ1\\n\\nI have resolved:\\nU1 -> imports/BQ7961