                             internal rails (`AVDD`, `CVDD`, `DVDD`). It features a daisy-chainable communication                      
                             interface (`COMH`/`COML`) and a local UART/SPI interface (`RX`/`TX`).\n    10\t5.                         
                             **Auxiliary Measurement Inputs:** The system includes two configurable paths for driving the              
                             `BBP` and `BBN` pins (Pins 64/63) of the BMS IC. These pins are typically used for auxiliary              
                             voltage measurements. The two options are:\n    11\t    *   **Bus Bar Measurement (DNP):**                
