                             465\t\u251c\u2500\u2500 tests/\n   466\t\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 mcp/                                  
                             # MCP server tests\n   467\t\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 library/                  #                       
                             Validation tests\n   468\t\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 docker/                   # Docker                  
                             integration tests\n   469\t\u251c\u2500\u2500 Dockerfile                    # Docker image                
                             definition\n   470\t\u251c\u2500\u2500 docker-compose.yml            # Docker Compose                     
                             configuration\n   471\t\u2514\u2500\u2500 package.json                  # Dependencies and                
                             scripts\n   472\t```\n   473\t\n   474\t### Component Lifecycle\n   475\t\n   476\t1.                     
                             **Search**: Agent searches for components using `search_library`\n   477\t2. **Generate**: If             
                             not found, agent generates component code\n   478\t3. **Stage**: Component is written to                  
                             temporary directory\n   479\t4. **Validate**: TypeScript compilation and dependency checks\n              
                             480\t5. **Commit**: If valid, moved to local library directory\n   481\t6. **Cleanup**:                   
                             Temporary files removed\n   482\t\n   483\t### Transport Abstraction\n   484\t\n   485\tThe               
                             MCP server core is transport-agnostic:\n   486\t- **stdio**: Used for local development and               
                             testing\n   487\t- **HTTP**: Used for Docker deployment\n   488\t- Both transports use the                
                             same tool handlers and validation logic\n   489\t\n   490\t## \ud83e\uddea Development\n                  
                             491\t\n   492\t### Project Setup\n   493\t\n   494\t```bash\n   495\t# Clone the repository\n             
                             496\tgit clone <repository-url>\n   497\tcd virtual_hardware_laboratory\n   498\t\n   499\t#              
                             Install dependencies\n   500\tpnpm install\n   501\t\n   502\t# Build the project\n                       
                             503\tpnpm build\n   504\t```\n   505\t\n   506\t### Running Tests\n   507\t\n                             
                             508\t```bash\n   509\t# Run all tests\n   510\tpnpm test\n   511\t\n   512\t# Run specific                
                             test suite\n   513\tpnpm test tests/mcp/server.test.ts\n   514\t\n   515\t# Run with                      
                             coverage\n   516\tpnpm test --coverage\n   517\t```\n   518\t\n   519\t### Local Development              
                             Workflow\n   520\t\n   521\t1. **Make changes** to source code in `src/`\n   522\t2. **Run                
                             tests** to validate: `pnpm test`\n   523\t3. **Build** the project: `pnpm build`\n   524\t4.              
                             **Test locally** with stdio: `pnpm run dev`\n   525\t5. **Test Docker build**: `docker build              
                             -t vhl-library .`\n   526\t6. **Test Docker run**: `docker run -p 8080:8080 vhl-library`\n                
                             527\t\n   528\t### Adding New Tools\n   529\t\n   530\tTo add a new MCP tool:\n   531\t\n                 
                             532\t1. Create tool handler in `src/mcp/tools/`\n   533\t2. Define input schema and response              
                             type\n   534\t3. Implement validation logic\n   535\t4. Register in `src/mcp/server.ts`:\n                
                             536\t   - Add to `ListToolsRequestSchema` handler\n   537\t   - Add to                                    
                             `CallToolRequestSchema` dispatcher\n   538\t5. Add tests in `tests/mcp/`\n   539\t\n                      
                             540\t### Code Style\n   541\t\n   542\t- TypeScript strict mode enabled\n   543\t- ES modules             
                             (ESM) throughout\n   544\t- Async/await for asynchronous operations\n   545\t- Comprehensive              
                             error handling\n   546\t\n   547\t## \ud83d\udc1b Troubleshooting\n   548\t\n   549\t###                  
                             Common Issues\n   550\t\n   551\t#### \"MCP stdio server cannot run in TTY mode\"\n   552\t\n             
                             553\t**Cause**: Running the server directly in a terminal with stdio transport.\n   554\t\n               
                             555\t**Solution**: Either:\n   556\t- Use HTTP transport: `VHL_TRANSPORT=http pnpm start`\n               
                             557\t- Run via MCP client that pipes stdin/stdout\n   558\t- Use Docker deployment\n                      
                             559\t\n   560\t#### Port Already in Use\n   561\t\n   562\t**Cause**: Port 8080 is occupied               
                             by another service.\n   563\t\n   564\t**Solution**:\n   565\t```bash\n   566\t# Check what's             
                             using the port\n   567\tlsof -i :8080\n   568\t\n   569\t# Use a different port\n                         
                             570\tdocker run -p 9090:8080 -e PORT=8080 vhl-library\n   571\t```\n   572\t\n   573\t####                
                             Component Validation Fails\n   574\t\n   575\t**Cause**: TypeScript compilation errors or                 
                             missing dependencies.\n   576\t\n   577\t**Solution**: Check the error messages in the                    
                             response:\n   578\t```typescript\n   579\t{\n   580\t  \"success\": false,\n   581\t                      
                             \"errors\": [\n   582\t    \"Imported footprint not found in library: custom.kicad_mod.                   
                             Please upload it first.\"\n   583\t  ]\n   584\t}\n   585\t```\n   586\t\n   587\tAdd                     
                             dependencies first, then retry.\n   588\t\n   589\t#### Docker Container Won't Start\n                    
                             590\t\n   591\t**Cause**: Various issues (port conflict, build failure, etc.)\n   592\t\n                 
                             593\t**Solution**:\n   594\t```bash\n   595\t# Check container logs\n   596\tdocker logs                  
                             vhl-library\n   597\t\n   598\t# Check container status\n   599\tdocker ps -a\n   600\t\n                 
                             601\t# Rebuild image\n   602\tdocker-compose build --no-cache\n   603\tdocker-compose up\n                
                             604\t```\n   605\t\n   606\t#### Volume Data Lost\n   607\t\n   608\t**Cause**: Using                     
                             anonymous volumes or removing named volumes.\n   609\t\n   610\t**Solution**: Always use                  
                             named volumes in production:\n   611\t```yaml\n   612\tvolumes:\n   613\t  vhl-lib:\n   614\t             
                             driver: local\n   615\t```\n   616\t\n   617\tBackup regularly:\n   618\t```bash\n                        
                             619\tdocker run --rm -v vhl-lib:/data -v $(pwd):/backup alpine \\\n   620\t  tar czf                      
                             /backup/vhl-backup.tar.gz -C /data .\n   621\t```\n   622\t\n   623\t### Debug Mode\n                     
                             624\t\n   625\tEnable verbose logging:\n   626\t\n   627\t```bash\n   628\t# Local\n                      
                             629\tDEBUG=* pnpm run dev\n   630\t\n   631\t# Docker\n   632\tdocker run -e DEBUG=* -p                   
                             8080:8080 vhl-library\n   633\t```\n   634\t\n   635\t### Health Checks\n   636\t\n                       
                             637\t```bash\n   638\t# HTTP health endpoint\n   639\tcurl http://localhost:8080/health\n                 
                             640\t\n   641\t# List tools\n   642\tcurl -X POST http://localhost:8080/mcp \\\n   643\t  -H              
                             \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n   644\t  -d                                                       
                             '{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"tools/list\"}'\n   645\t\n   646\t# Check Docker              
                             container health\n   647\tdocker inspect vhl-library | grep Health\n   648\t```\n   649\t\n               
