'{"command": "view", "security_risk": "LOW", "path": "/home/pst/Documents/vhl_librarian/virtual_hardware_laboratary/docs/vhl_library_readme.md"}'}}]}, {'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'Your thought has been logged.'}], 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_0cdbcb1d53e54d74aede6224050f', 'name': 'think'}, {'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'Here\'s the result of running `cat -n` on /home/pst/Documents/vhl_librarian/virtual_hardware_laboratary/docs/vhl_library_readme.md:\n     1\t# Virtual Hardware Laboratory (VHL) 🔧\n     2\t\n     3\tA TypeScript-based Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for tscircuit-driven hardware design. VHL enables LLM agents to search, validate, and manage hardware components through a standardized API.\n     4\t\n     5\t## 🎯 Overview\n     6\t\n     7\tVHL Library provides:\n     8\t\n     9\t- **Component Management**: Add, validate, and store TSX components and KiCAD footprints\n    10\t- **Library Search**: Search both local and global (tscircuit) component libraries\n    11\t- **Dual Transport**: Run locally via stdio or as a Docker service via HTTP\n    12\t- **Automatic Validation**: TypeScript compilation and dependency checking\n    13\t- **MCP Protocol**: Standardized interface for AI agent integration\n    14\t\n    15\t## ⚡ Quick Start\n    16\t\n    17\t### Local Development (stdio)\n    18\t\n    19\t```bash\n    20\t# Install dependencies\n    21\tpnpm install\n    22\t\n    23\t# Run the MCP server\n    24\tpnpm run dev\n    25\t\n    26\t# Run tests\n    27\tpnpm test\n    28\t```\n    29\t\n    30\t### Docker Deployment (HTTP)\n    31\t\n    32\t```bash\n    33\t# Using Docker Compose (Recommended)\n    34\tdocker-compose up -d\n    35\t\n    36\t# The service will be available at:\n    37\t# http://localhost:8080/mcp\n    38\t\n    39\t# View logs\n    40\tdocker-compose logs -f\n    41\t\n    42\t# Stop the service\n    43\tdocker-compose down\n    44\t```\n    45\t\n    46\t## 🐳 Docker Container Setup\n    47\t\n    48\t### Prerequisites\n    49\t\n    50\t- Docker and Docker Compose installed\n    51\t- Node.js 20+ (for local development)\n    52\t\n    53\t### Build and Run\n    54\t\n    55\t#### Option 1: Docker Compose\n    56\t\n    57\t```bash\n    58\t# Build and start\n    59\tdocker-compose up -d\n    60\t\n    61\t# Check status\n    62\tdocker-compose ps\n    63\t\n    64\t# View logs\n    65\tdocker-compose logs -f vhl-library\n    66\t\n    67\t# Stop and remove\n    68\tdocker-compose down\n    69\t```\n    70\t\n    71\t#### Option 2: Docker CLI\n    72\t\n    73\t```bash\n    74\t# Build the image\n    75\tdocker build -t vhl-library .\n    76\t\n    77\t# Run the container\n    78\tdocker run -d \\\n    79\t  --name vhl-library \\\n    80\t  -p 8080:8080 \\\n    81\t  -v vhl-lib:/app/lib \\\n    82\t  -e VHL_TRANSPORT=http \\\n    83\t  -e PORT=8080 \\\n    84\t  vhl-library\n    85\t\n    86\t# Check health\n    87\tcurl http://localhost:8080/health\n    88\t\n    89\t# View logs\n    90\tdocker logs -f vhl-library\n    91\t\n    92\t# Stop and remove\n    93\tdocker stop vhl-library && docker rm vhl-library\n    94\t```\n    95\t\n    96\t### Environment Variables\n    97\t\n    98\t| Variable | Default | Description |\n    99\t|----------|---------|-------------|\n   100\t| `VHL_TRANSPORT` | `stdio` | Transport mode: `stdio` (local) or `http` (Docker) |\n   101\t| `PORT` | `8080` | HTTP server port (only for http transport) |\n   102\t| `VHL_LIBRARY_DIR` | `/app/lib` | Directory for persistent component storage |\n   103\t\n   104\t### Volume Persistence\n   105\t\n   106\tThe Docker container uses a named volume (`vhl-lib`) to persist components:\n   107\t\n   108\t```bash\n   109\t# Inspect the volume\n   110\tdocker volume inspect vhl-lib\n   111\t\n   112\t# Backup the volume\n   113\tdocker run --rm -v vhl-lib:/data -v $(pwd):/backup alpine tar czf /backup/vhl-backup.tar.gz -C /data .\n   114\t\n   115\t# Restore from backup\n   116\tdocker run --rm -v vhl-lib:/data -v $(pwd):/backup alpine tar xzf /backup/vhl-backup.tar.gz -C /data\n   117\t```\n   118\t\n   119\t## 📡 MCP Server API Reference\n   120\t\n   121\tThe VHL Library implements the Model Context Protocol (MCP) and exposes three tools via JSON-RPC 2.0.\n   122\t\n   123\t### Transport Modes\n   124\t\n   125\t#### stdio Transport (Local Development)\n   126\t- Used by default when running locally\n   127\t- Communication via stdin/stdout\n   128\t- Best for testing, CI, and local development\n   129\t\n   130\t#### HTTP Transport (Docker)\n   131\t- Enabled when `VHL_TRANSPORT=http`\n   132\t- RESTful JSON-RPC endpoint at `POST /mcp`\n   133\t- Health check endpoint at `GET /health`\n   134\t- Best for production deployments and remote access\n   135\t\n   136\t### Tool 1: `add_component`\n   137\t\n   138\tAdd or update a TSX component or KiCAD footprint in the local library.\n   139\t\n   140\t**Input Schema:**\n   141\t```json\n   142\t{\n   143\t  "component_name": "string (required)",\n   144\t  "file_content": "string (required)"\n   145\t}\n   146\t```\n   147\t\n   148\t**Parameters:**\n   149\t- `component_name`: Component name (e.g., `MyResistor`) or filename with extension (e.g., `footprint.kicad_mod`)\n   150\t  - For TSX files: Name will have `.tsx` appended if not specified\n   151\t  - For KiCAD files: Must end with `.kicad_mod`\n   152\t- `file_content`: Complete file content (TSX or KiCAD footprint format)\n   153\t\n   154\t**Validation Rules:**\n   155\t- TSX files must be valid TypeScript with JSX\n   156\t- TSX files must export at least one symbol\n   157\t- TSX files importing `.kicad_mod` files must have those footprints already in the library\n   158\t- KiCAD `.kicad_mod` files are accepted without compilation validation\n   159\t\n   160\t**Response:**\n   161\t```json\n   162\t{\n   163\t  "success": true,\n   164\t  "componentPath": "/app/lib/MyResistor.tsx"\n   165\t}\n   166\t```\n   167\t\n   168\t**Error Response:**\n   169\t```json\n   170\t{\n   171\t  "success": false,\n   172\t  "errors": [\n   173\t    "Component must export at least one symbol"\n   174\t  ]\n   175\t}\n   176\t```\n   177\t\n   178\t**Example (HTTP):**\n   179\t```bash\n   180\tcurl -X POST http://localhost:8080/mcp \\\n   181\t  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\\n   182\t  -d \'{\n   183\t    "jsonrpc": "2.0",\n   184\t    "id": 1,\n   185\t    "method": "tools/call",\n   186\t    "params": {\n   187\t      "name": "add_component",\n   188\t      "arguments": {\n   189\t        "component_name": "MyResistor",\n   190\t        "file_content": "import { resistor } from \\"@tsci/seveibar.resistor\\";\\n\\nexport const MyResistor = (props: { resistance: string }) => {\\n  return <resistor resistance={props.resistance} />;\\n};"\n   191\t      }\n   192\t    }\n   193\t  }\'\n   194\t```\n   195\t\n   196\t### Tool 2: `list_local_components`\n   197\t\n   198\tList all components in the local library.\n   199\t\n   200\t**Input Schema:**\n   201\t```json\n   202\t{}\n   203\t```\n   204\t\n   205\t**Response:**\n   206\t```json\n   207\t[\n   208\t  {\n   209\t    "name": "MyResistor",\n   210\t    "file": "MyResistor.tsx"\n   211\t  },\n   212\t  {\n   213\t    "name": "MyCapacitor",\n   214\t    "file": "MyCapacitor.tsx"\n   215\t  }\n   216\t]\n   217\t```\n   218\t\n   219\t**Example (HTTP):**\n   220\t```bash\n   221\tcurl -X POST http://localhost:8080/mcp \\\n   222\t  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\\n   223\t  -d \'{\n   224\t    "jsonrpc": "2.0",\n   225\t    "id": 2,\n   226\t    "method": "tools/call",\n   227\t    "params": {\n   228\t      "name": "list_local_components",\n   229\t      "arguments": {}\n   230\t    }\n   231\t  }\'\n   232\t```\n   233\t\n   234\t### Tool 3: `search_library`\n   235\t\n   236\tSearch both local and global (tscircuit registry) libraries for components.\n   237\t\n   238\t**Input Schema:**\n   239\t```json\n   240\t{\n   241\t  "query": "string (required)",\n   242\t  "mode": "fuzzy | regex (required)",\n   243\t  "depth": "surface | deep (required)"\n   244\t}\n   245\t```\n   246\t\n   247\t**Parameters:**\n   248\t- `query`: Search query string\n   249\t- `mode`: \n   250\t  - `fuzzy`: Case-insensitive substring matching\n   251\t  - `regex`: Regular expression pattern matching\n   252\t- `depth`:\n   253\t  - `surface`: Returns only name and source\n   254\t  - `deep`: Returns name, source, and additional metadata (exports, pins)\n   255\t\n   256\t**Response (surface):**\n   257\t```json\n   258\t[\n   259\t  {\n   260\t    "name": "MyResistor",\n   261\t    "source": "local",\n   262\t    "description": "Custom resistor component"\n   263\t  },\n   264\t  {\n   265\t    "name": "seveibar.resistor",\n   266\t    "source": "global",\n   267\t    "description": "Standard resistor - Stars: 42"\n   268\t  }\n   269\t]\n   270\t```\n   271\t\n   272\t**Response (deep):**\n   273\t```json\n   274\t[\n   275\t  {\n   276\t    "name": "MyResistor",\n   277\t    "source": "local",\n   278\t    "exports": ["default"]\n   279\t  },\n   280\t  {\n   281\t    "name": "seveibar.resistor",\n   282\t    "source": "global",\n   283\t    "description": "Standard resistor",\n   284\t    "exports": ["default"]\n   285\t  }\n   286\t]\n   287\t```\n   288\t\n   289\t**Example (HTTP):**\n   290\t```bash\n   291\tcurl -X POST http://localhost:8080/mcp \\\n   292\t  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\\n   293\t  -d \'{\n   294\t    "jsonrpc": "2.0",\n   295\t    "id": 3,\n   296\t    "method": "tools/call",\n   297\t    "params": {\n   298\t      "name": "search_library",\n   299\t      "arguments": {\n   300\t        "query": "resistor",\n   301\t        "mode": "fuzzy",\n   302\t        "depth": "surface"\n   303\t      }\n   304\t    }\n   305\t  }\'\n   306\t```\n   307\t\n   308\t### List Available Tools\n   309\t\n   310\tQuery the server for all available tools:\n   311\t\n   312\t**Request:**\n   313\t```bash\n   314\tcurl -X POST http://localhost:8080/mcp \\\n   315\t  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\\n   316\t  -d \'{\n   317\t    "jsonrpc": "2.0",\n   318\t    "id": 0,\n   319\t    "method": "tools/list"\n   320\t  }\'\n   321\t```\n   322\t\n   323\t**Response:**\n   324\t```json\n   325\t{\n   326\t  "jsonrpc": "2.0",\n   327\t  "id": 0,\n   328\t  "result": {\n   329\t    "tools": [\n   330\t      {\n   331\t        "name": "add_component",\n   332\t        "description": "Add or update a TSX component or KiCAD footprint (.kicad_mod) in the local library. Validation is automatic.",\n   333\t        "inputSchema": { ... }\n   334\t      },\n   335\t      {\n   336\t        "name": "list_local_components",\n   337\t        "description": "List components explicitly added to the local library.",\n   338\t        "inputSchema": { ... }\n   339\t      },\n   340\t      {\n   341\t        "name": "search_library",\n   342\t        "description": "Search local and global libraries for components.",\n   343\t        "inputSchema": { ... }\n   344\t      }\n   345\t    ]\n   346\t  }\n   347\t}\n   348\t```\n   349\t\n   350\t## 🤖 LLM Agent Integration Guide\n   351\t\n   352\t### Overview\n   353\t\n   354\tVHL Library is designed to be used by LLM agents to manage hardware components. The MCP protocol provides a standardized interface that agents can use to:\n   355\t\n   356\t1. Search for components in local and global libraries\n   357\t2. Add new components with automatic validation\n   358\t3. List existing local components\n   359\t4. Manage component dependencies\n   360\t\n   361\t### Integration Steps\n   362\t\n   363\t#### Step <response clipped><NOTE>Due to the max output limit, only part of this file has been shown to you. You should retry this tool after you have searched inside the file with `grep -n` in order to find the line numbers of what you are looking for.</NOTE>ponentName(generatedCode),\n   364\t      file_content: generatedCode\n   365\t    });\n   366\t\n   367\t    // 5. Handle validation errors\n   368\t    if (!result.success) {\n   369\t      // Retry with fixed code\n   370\t      const fixedCode = await this.fixValidationErrors(\n   371\t        generatedCode,\n   372\t        result.errors\n   373\t      );\n   374\t      \n   375\t      return await callMCPTool(\'add_component\', {\n   376\t        component_name: this.extractComponentName(fixedCode),\n   377\t        file_content: fixedCode\n   378\t      });\n   379\t    }\n   380\t\n   381\t    return { created: true, path: result.componentPath };\n   382\t  }\n   383\t}\n   384\t```\n   385\t\n   386\t### Testing Your Agent\n   387\t\n   388\tUse the provided test suite as a reference:\n   389\t\n   390\t```bash\n   391\t# Run MCP server tests\n   392\tpnpm test tests/mcp/\n   393\t\n   394\t# Run Docker integration tests\n   395\tpnpm test tests/docker/\n   396\t```\n   397\t\n   398\t## 🏗️ Architecture\n   399\t\n   400\t### System Overview\n   401\t\n   402\t```\n   403\t┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n   404\t│            LLM Agent / Client               │\n   405\t│                                             │\n   406\t│  • Component search & discovery             │\n   407\t│  • Component generation                     │\n   408\t│  • Validation & error handling              │\n   409\t└─────────────────┬───────────────────────────┘\n   410\t                  │\n   411\t                  │ MCP Protocol (JSON-RPC 2.0)\n   412\t                  │\n   413\t        ┌─────────┴──────────┐\n   414\t        │                    │\n   415\t    stdio (local)       HTTP (Docker)\n   416\t        │                    │\n   417\t        └─────────┬──────────┘\n   418\t                  │\n   419\t┌─────────────────▼───────────────────────────┐\n   420\t│         VHL Library MCP Server              │\n   421\t│                                             │\n   422\t│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐   │\n   423\t│  │  Tool Handlers                      │   │\n   424\t│  │  • add_component                    │   │\n   425\t│  │  • list_local_components            │   │\n   426\t│  │  • search_library                   │   │\n   427\t│  └─────────────────────────────────────┘   │\n   428\t│                                             │\n   429\t│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐   │\n   430\t│  │  Validation Engine                  │   │\n   431\t│  │  • TypeScript compilation           │   │\n   432\t│  │  • Export detection                 │   │\n   433\t│  │  • Dependency checking              │   │\n   434\t│  └─────────────────────────────────────┘   │\n   435\t│                                             │\n   436\t│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐   │\n   437\t│  │  Library Manager                    │   │\n   438\t│  │  • Local library (filesystem)       │   │\n   439\t│  │  • Global search (tscircuit CLI)    │   │\n   440\t│  └─────────────────────────────────────┘   │\n   441\t└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n   442\t```\n   443\t\n   444\t### Directory Structure\n   445\t\n   446\t```\n   447\tvirtual_hardware_laboratory/\n   448\t├── src/\n   449\t│   ├── config/\n   450\t│   │   └── paths.ts              # Path configuration\n   451\t│   ├── library/\n   452\t│   │   ├── local/                # Local component storage\n   453\t│   │   └── validator.ts          # Component validation logic\n   454\t│   ├── mcp/\n   455\t│   │   ├── server.ts             # MCP server core\n   456\t│   │   ├── tools/\n   457\t│   │   │   ├── addComponent.ts   # Add component tool\n   458\t│   │   │   ├── listLocal.ts      # List local components tool\n   459\t│   │   │   └── searchLibrary.ts  # Search library tool\n   460\t│   │   └── transport/\n   461\t│   │       └── HttpServerTransport.ts  # HTTP transport\n   462\t│   ├── runtime/\n   463\t│   │   └── libraryFs.ts          # Filesystem operations\n   464\t│   └── index.ts                  # Application entry point\n   465\t├── tests/\n   466\t│   ├── mcp/                      # MCP server tests\n   467\t│   ├── library/                  # Validation tests\n   468\t│   └── docker/                   # Docker integration tests\n   469\t├── Dockerfile                    # Docker image definition\n   470\t├── docker-compose.yml            # Docker Compose configuration\n   471\t└── package.json                  # Dependencies and scripts\n   472\t```\n   473\t\n   474\t### Component Lifecycle\n   475\t\n   476\t1. **Search**: Agent searches for components using `search_library`\n   477\t2. **Generate**: If not found, agent generates component code\n   478\t3. **Stage**: Component is written to temporary directory\n   479\t4. **Validate**: TypeScript compilation and dependency checks\n   480\t5. **Commit**: If valid, moved to local library directory\n   481\t6. **Cleanup**: Temporary files removed\n   482\t\n   483\t### Transport Abstraction\n   484\t\n   485\tThe MCP server core is transport-agnostic:\n   486\t- **stdio**: Used for local development and testing\n   487\t- **HTTP**: Used for Docker deployment\n   488\t- Both transports use the same tool handlers and validation logic\n   489\t\n   490\t## 🧪 Development\n   491\t\n   492\t### Project Setup\n   493\t\n   494\t```bash\n   495\t# Clone the repository\n   496\tgit clone <repository-url>\n   497\tcd virtual_hardware_laboratory\n   498\t\n   499\t# Install dependencies\n   500\tpnpm install\n   501\t\n   502\t# Build the project\n   503\tpnpm build\n   504\t```\n   505\t\n   506\t### Running Tests\n   507\t\n   508\t```bash\n   509\t# Run all tests\n   510\tpnpm test\n   511\t\n   512\t# Run specific test suite\n   513\tpnpm test tests/mcp/server.test.ts\n   514\t\n   515\t# Run with coverage\n   516\tpnpm test --coverage\n   517\t```\n   518\t\n   519\t### Local Development Workflow\n   520\t\n   521\t1. **Make changes** to source code in `src/`\n   522\t2. **Run tests** to validate: `pnpm test`\n   523\t3. **Build** the project: `pnpm build`\n   524\t4. **Test locally** with stdio: `pnpm run dev`\n   525\t5. **Test Docker build**: `docker build -t vhl-library .`\n   526\t6. **Test Docker run**: `docker run -p 8080:8080 vhl-library`\n   527\t\n   528\t### Adding New Tools\n   529\t\n   530\tTo add a new MCP tool:\n   531\t\n   532\t1. Create tool handler in `src/mcp/tools/`\n   533\t2. Define input schema and response type\n   534\t3. Implement validation logic\n   535\t4. Register in `src/mcp/server.ts`:\n   536\t   - Add to `ListToolsRequestSchema` handler\n   537\t   - Add to `CallToolRequestSchema` dispatcher\n   538\t5. Add tests in `tests/mcp/`\n   539\t\n   540\t### Code Style\n   541\t\n   542\t- TypeScript strict mode enabled\n   543\t- ES modules (ESM) throughout\n   544\t- Async/await for asynchronous operations\n   545\t- Comprehensive error handling\n   546\t\n   547\t## 🐛 Troubleshooting\n   548\t\n   549\t### Common Issues\n   550\t\n   551\t#### "MCP stdio server cannot run in TTY mode"\n   552\t\n   553\t**Cause**: Running the server directly in a terminal with stdio transport.\n   554\t\n   555\t**Solution**: Either:\n   556\t- Use HTTP transport: `VHL_TRANSPORT=http pnpm start`\n   557\t- Run via MCP client that pipes stdin/stdout\n   558\t- Use Docker deployment\n   559\t\n   560\t#### Port Already in Use\n   561\t\n   562\t**Cause**: Port 8080 is occupied by another service.\n   563\t\n   564\t**Solution**:\n   565\t```bash\n   566\t# Check what\'s using the port\n   567\tlsof -i :8080\n   568\t\n   569\t# Use a different port\n   570\tdocker run -p 9090:8080 -e PORT=8080 vhl-library\n   571\t```\n   572\t\n   573\t#### Component Validation Fails\n   574\t\n   575\t**Cause**: TypeScript compilation errors or missing dependencies.\n   576\t\n   577\t**Solution**: Check the error messages in the response:\n   578\t```typescript\n   579\t{\n   580\t  "success": false,\n   581\t  "errors": [\n   582\t    "Imported footprint not found in library: custom.kicad_mod. Please upload it first."\n   583\t  ]\n   584\t}\n   585\t```\n   586\t\n   587\tAdd dependencies first, then retry.\n   588\t\n   589\t#### Docker Container Won\'t Start\n   590\t\n   591\t**Cause**: Various issues (port conflict, build failure, etc.)\n   592\t\n   593\t**Solution**:\n   594\t```bash\n   595\t# Check container logs\n   596\tdocker logs vhl-library\n   597\t\n   598\t# Check container status\n   599\tdocker ps -a\n   600\t\n   601\t# Rebuild image\n   602\tdocker-compose build --no-cache\n   603\tdocker-compose up\n   604\t```\n   605\t\n   606\t#### Volume Data Lost\n   607\t\n   608\t**Cause**: Using anonymous volumes or removing named volumes.\n   609\t\n   610\t**Solution**: Always use named volumes in production:\n   611\t```yaml\n   612\tvolumes:\n   613\t  vhl-lib:\n   614\t    driver: local\n   615\t```\n   616\t\n   617\tBackup regularly:\n   618\t```bash\n   619\tdocker run --rm -v vhl-lib:/data -v $(pwd):/backup alpine \\\n   620\t  tar czf /backup/vhl-backup.tar.gz -C /data .\n   621\t```\n   622\t\n   623\t### Debug Mode\n   624\t\n   625\tEnable verbose logging:\n   626\t\n   627\t```bash\n   628\t# Local\n   629\tDEBUG=* pnpm run dev\n   630\t\n   631\t# Docker\n   632\tdocker run -e DEBUG=* -p 8080:8080 vhl-library\n   633\t```\n   634\t\n   635\t### Health Checks\n   636\t\n   637\t```bash\n   638\t# HTTP health endpoint\n   639\tcurl http://localhost:8080/health\n   640\t\n   641\t# List tools\n   642\tcurl -X POST http://localhost:8080/mcp \\\n   643\t  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\\n   644\t  -d \'{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/list"}\'\n   645\t\n   646\t# Check Docker container health\n   647\tdocker inspect vhl-library | grep Health\n   648\t```\n   649\t\n   650\t## 📚 Additional Resources\n   651\t\n   652\t- [Model Context Protocol (MCP) Documentation](https://modelcontextprotocol.io)\n   653\t- [tscircuit Documentation](https://docs.tscircuit.com)\n   654\t- [TypeScript Handbook](https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/)\n   655\t- [Docker Documentation](https://docs.docker.com)\n   656\t\n   657\t## 📝 License\n   658\t\n   659\t[Your License Here]\n   660\t\n   661\t## 🤝 Contributing\n   662\t\n   663\tContributions are welcome! Please:\n   664\t\n   665\t1. Fork the repository\n   666\t2. Create a feature branch\n   667\t3. Make your changes with tests\n   668\t4. Submit a pull request\n   669\t\n   670\t## 📧 Support\n   671\t\n   672\tFor issues and questions:\n   673\t- Open an issue on GitHub\n   674\t- Check existing documentation in `/docs`\n   675\t- Review test files for usage examples\n   676\t\n'}], 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_320442f8987d42bf85d495fbceaf', 'name': 'file_editor'}], 'thinking': None, 'web_search_options': None, 'safety_identifier': None, 'service_tier': None}
